/*
  holdings: a claim to hold a Bitcraft item, proved without showing the item.

  Holds(state_header, type, nullifier, tag) says the prover knows an object
  state `obj` such that:

  - its commitment is in the created array of `state_header`, whose hash is a
    state root. The synchronizer only adds commitments from valid
    `TxFinalized` proofs, so a valid transaction made `obj`, under the rules
    of the class whose `Is<Class>` predicate hash is `type`;
  - `nullifier` is the spend tag the network records when `obj` is consumed,
    H(H(obj, obj.key), "txlib-nullifier-v1") as in txlib.podlang. Only a
    holder of `obj.key` can compute it;
  - `tag` is H(obj.stable_identifier, "bitcraft-holdings-v1"). Every state of
    an object keeps its stable_identifier (TxInsert stamps it, TxMutate and
    Rekey keep it), so the tag stays the same when the object is re-keyed or
    changed, and a leaderboard can count each object once.

  Whether `obj` is still live is for the verifier to ask the network: it is
  live while `nullifier` is not in the nullifier set.

  The StateHeader record matches txlib's (txlib.podlang, `record StateHeader`).
*/

record StateHeader = (block_number, block_timestamp, block_hash, created, nullifiers, prior_state_history)

Holds(state_header StateHeader, type, nullifier, tag, private: obj, index, obj_key_hash) = AND(
  ArrayContains(state_header.created, index, obj)
  DictContains(obj, "type", type)
  Hash(obj, obj.key, obj_key_hash)
  Hash(obj_key_hash, "txlib-nullifier-v1", nullifier)
  Hash(obj.stable_identifier, "bitcraft-holdings-v1", tag)
)
